# Yespizz implementation workflow

The canonical engineering task queue is `docs/IMPLEMENTATION-BACKLOG.md`.

When asked to continue, complete, or implement the app:

1. Read `docs/PRODUCT.md`, `prd/product-strategy.md`, and
   `docs/IMPLEMENTATION-BACKLOG.md` before editing.
2. Select the first unchecked task whose dependencies are complete unless the user
   names a specific task ID.
3. Implement only one task per coherent change/PR.
4. Treat Release blocker and P0 acceptance criteria as mandatory.
5. Preserve the backend invariants: blind provider identity, server-owned pricing and
   dispatch, batch size at most three, and proof-required delivery transitions.
6. Update backend DTOs and `packages/api` DTOs/clients together.
7. Add negative authorization and invalid-transition tests for every privileged or
   state-changing endpoint.
8. Never ship demo coordinates, fake success paths, mock OTPs, raw card collection,
   or local-only chat/call behavior as production functionality.
9. Run the checks required by the task and the global Definition of Done.
10. Mark the task complete only after showing test evidence; record any follow-up as a
    new backlog item instead of silently expanding scope.

If docs and code disagree, inspect tests and implementation, then update the stale
documentation in the same change.

